1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
TEN (ENVELOPE)

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Ten:

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The ability to envelop your body
in a shroud of Nen aura,

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
making it tougher and slowing
the effects of aging.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
ZETSU (SUPPRESS)

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Zetsu: A technique which
shuts off your flow of Nen aura.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Effective for concealing your presence
and recovering from fatigue.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
REN (REFINE)

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Ren: A technique for creating
an especially strong Nen aura.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It is crucial for increasing your power.

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,000
HATSU (RELEASE)

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hatsu: The release of your Nen aura,
after using Ren to boost it.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
These four elements are known
as the Four Exercises

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
and are critical to the mastery of Nen.

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
FOUR EXERCISES

16
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
[theme song playing]

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
[cheering]

18
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[Gon] I’m really sorry, Mr. Wing.

19
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
But I’m itching for a fight right now!

20
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
FIERCE x AND x FEROCIOUS

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
[narrator] Gon faces his first match
on the 200th floor,

22
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
but is caught off guard
by his opponent’s unconventional attack.

23
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
[cackling]

24
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
[cries out in pain]

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
And another top hits him from behind!

26
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
It looks like he’s in big trouble now

27
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
because he’s just been surrounded
by the Dancing Tops!

28
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
[grunts]

29
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
[grunts]

30
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
[cries out in pain]

31
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
That’s a clean hit and knockdown!

32
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
For two points!

33
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
[commentator]
Gido’s up to an early four-point lead!

34
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
-Can you fight?
-You bet!

35
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
There are too many tops for me

36
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
to be able to keep track of all of them.
Dammit!

37
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
What should I do?

38
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
[Zushi] M-- Master…

39
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Is he using Nen right now?

40
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[Wing] Yes. That’s a form of Hatsu.

41
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
He’s projecting his aura into the tops.

42
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
That is what allows the tops

43
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
to move around with significantly
more strength and speed

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
than would normally be possible.

45
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
[Wing] Small objects require
only a small amount of aura.

46
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
The larger the object,
the more aura is necessary.

47
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
And I wouldn’t be surprised

48
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
if Gido gave the tops
extra Nen for good measure.

49
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
That’s because
letting the tops spin on their own

50
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
without the benefit of additional aura,
wouldn’t pack much of a punch.

51
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
He can do this

52
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
because he feels great personal affinity
with them.

53
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Nothing has more of an impact
on an object’s response

54
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
than strong emotional attachment.

55
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
[grunting]

56
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
I can’t follow them with my eyes.

57
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
The tops have been charged with Nen.

58
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
I have to sense their presence!

59
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Yeah. I feel it!

60
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
My Ten is fading!

61
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
[groans]

62
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[commentator] Another direct hit!

63
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Gon is completely helpless!

64
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
He’s been knocked clear out of the ring!

65
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
[Gon grunts]

66
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
[commentator] The score is now six-zero!

67
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
He’s dug himself quite a hole!

68
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
[Gon] It’s no use.

69
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
If I focus on sensing the tops,

70
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
I neglect my Ten and it seeps away…

71
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
So, what should I--?

72
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
A top bounced outside the ring…

73
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
But... it’s not attacking me…

74
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
What's wrong?
Can you continue on with the match?

75
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Be quiet, okay?

76
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
I’m trying to think here!

77
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
If you’re not back in the ring
by the count of ten, you lose!

78
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
One!

79
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Now that I think about it,

80
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
the Nen in this top didn’t feel malicious.

81
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
What about all the others?

82
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
They’re just spinning
around the ring randomly

83
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,000
and bumping into each other.

84
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Maybe the tops aren’t really
coming after me at all.

85
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Four!

86
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
How come you’re standing
outside of the ring?

87
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Because if I stayed up there in the ring,
I’d probably end up getting hurt, too!

88
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
-And Five!
-That’s it!

89
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
It’s just like a game of ‘sumo tops’!

90
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[Wing] It’s impossible to command
regular tops to move with precision.

91
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
It’s much more likely
that Gido commands them

92
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
to strike down anything in their way.

93
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
They spin around the ring,

94
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
striking anything unfortunate enough
to cross their paths.

95
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Seven!

96
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
If the tops aren’t aiming for me,

97
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
I don’t have to fear them so much!

98
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I can ignore them
and attack Gido directly!

99
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
[scoffs]

100
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[Gido] You may have figured out my tops,

101
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
but you still can’t land an attack on me!

102
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
[commentator] There it is!

103
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Gido’s special technique,
combining offense and defense!

104
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Tornado Top!

105
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
[screams]

106
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
[commentator]
Whoa! Gon gets hit with a vicious counter!

107
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Three points!

108
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
The judge has awarded
a critical hit and knockdown!

109
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Gido has nine points!

110
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Gon is on the brink of defeat!

111
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
[straining]

112
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[cackling]

113
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
[Gido] I turn into a top to protect myself

114
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
and let my Dancing Tops
handle the offense!

115
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
It’s a conservative strategy

116
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
but it’s effective
for racking up the points!

117
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
[Wing]
There are a number of ways to defeat Gido.

118
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
You can attack him until he tires
and his Ten begins to fade.

119
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Or you can use Hatsu
to overpower his defense.

120
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:09,000
Both of those methods would require
an extremely large amount of aura.

121
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
But Gon doesn’t know Ren yet…

122
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:15,000
the technique
for generating aura instantly.

123
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Learning how to create
large amounts of aura quickly

124
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
and how to channel it into attacks...

125
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
That requires endless training
and combat experience

126
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
in order to learn.

127
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Gon has neither.

128
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
He’d need five more years to fight Gido.

129
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
I’m sure that’s beginning to dawn on him.

130
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
What should I do?

131
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
How am I gonna prolong this match?

132
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
If he scores one more point,

133
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,000
it’s over.

134
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
But I want to keep fighting!

135
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
What can I do right now?

136
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
I got it.

137
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[mumbles]

138
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Gon!

139
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[Wing] He released his Ten?!

140
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
That’s so reckless!

141
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
But he didn’t just release it…

142
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
That’s…

143
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Zetsu!

144
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
The technique
for concealing your presence!

145
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,000
All the nodes are closed
and there is no aura!

146
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Even the normal,
faint leak of aura is closed off,

147
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
leaving him no defense against Nen!

148
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
I didn’t teach him Zetsu.

149
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Did he learn it before we met?

150
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
If that’s the case,

151
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
he wouldn’t know that this is Zetsu.

152
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
He probably picked it up naturally
on his own,

153
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
just like how beasts in nature
learn it to hunt their prey!

154
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
He certainly has incredible potential.

155
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
But why would he use it now… here?

156
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
You idiot!

157
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
What if you get hit by another Nen attack?

158
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Without protection,
that’ll totally mess you up!

159
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,000
[Gon] I know that.

160
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
But… if I’m gonna track
the tops’ complex movements

161
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
with only feelings to go on,

162
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
then I need to focus all of my senses.

163
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Could it be that he never intended
to win this match?

164
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
He’s risking everything…

165
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
He’s risking his own life…

166
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,000
to train?!

167
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
[cackling]

168
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
[Gido] Do you have a death wish, kid?

169
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Then here! Let me give you what you want!

170
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
[Gido] What?

171
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[cheering]

172
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
[commentator] Amazing!

173
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,000
That’s the first time Gon
has managed to evade an attack!

174
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[Gon] I can feel them.

175
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
I know where they’re heading!

176
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
This is all I can do right now.

177
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Just concentrate
on dodging my opponent’s attacks!

178
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[mumbles]

179
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
At least this way I can still fight!

180
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
[Killua] Your right radius and your ulna
were both broken.

181
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
A fractured humerus.

182
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Three broken ribs.

183
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Not to mention
twelve other minor fractures.

184
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
It’ll take four months to heal.

185
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
You moron!

186
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Sorry!

187
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[yells] Well, an apology isn’t gonna help!

188
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Don’t you have any brains in there
at all?!

189
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Didn’t you see what happened
to all the guys who went through it?

190
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
The Nen initiation?

191
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
One wrong move and you would have
ended up like them!

192
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
It coulda been a lot worse,
so you’re lucky.

193
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Man. How come you think

194
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Four-Eyes was training us
in the first place?

195
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[Gon] [chuckles nervously]
Still...

196
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
I had a feeling that it’d be okay.

197
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
I mean, sure, I took a few hits.

198
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
But he missed my vital spots,
so no big deal.

199
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
[groans]

200
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
[rasping in pain]

201
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[knocking]

202
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Come in!

203
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[Gon exhales in relief]

204
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Oh! Four-Eyes!

205
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[Gon] Uh, I’m sor--

206
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Apologizing to me isn't going to help!

207
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
What on earth were you thinking?!

208
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Didn’t you see the ones
who went through the Nen initiation?

209
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
You could easily
have ended up just like them!

210
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
[Killua]
Yeah. I just told him the same thing.

211
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
[Wing sighs]

212
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Honestly…

213
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I’m glad it wasn’t any worse.

214
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
[Gon] I’m sorry, Mr. Wing.

215
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
I really am.

216
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,000
-I’m not letting this slide.
-[Gon] Huh?

217
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Killua. Do you know when Gon
will be completely recovered?

218
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,000
The doctor said
it’d take about two months.

219
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[Wing] I see.

220
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Thanks a lot, Killua.

221
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
In that case,

222
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I won’t allow you to participate
in any matches for two months.

223
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Nor will I allow the study of or training
in the use of Nen.

224
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
If you choose not to abide
by these conditions,

225
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
then you will never
receive instruction from me again.

226
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Understand?

227
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:50,000
[Gon] Yes, sir. I’ll do as you say.

228
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
Your left hand.

229
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:57,000
This is a promise thread.

230
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Its purpose is to remind you
of the promise you made.

231
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Okay.

232
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Killua. A word.

233
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,000
[Wing] So tell me…

234
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
what is the true goal
that you and Gon are pursuing here?

235
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
[Killua]
Well, we don’t really have a goal.

236
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Before we ran into you and Zushi,

237
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
I just wanted to earn some quick cash.

238
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Gon wants to beat a guy named Hisoka,

239
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
so he’s here to train.

240
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,000
And that’s it.

241
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Everyone on the 200th floor

242
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
just wants to reach the top floor.

243
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
The Battle Olympia. Right?

244
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Yeah, I’m not too interested.

245
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
But Gon, though…

246
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Well… I’m not so sure.

247
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
He says he doesn’t care what happens,

248
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
as long as he gets to fight Hisoka.

249
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
But after yesterday’s match…

250
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
I don't know.

251
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
I get the feeling
he just enjoys the thrill.

252
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
[cheering]

253
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[commentator] How long this back-and-forth
is going to go on

254
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
is anybody’s guess!

255
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
There are nearly fifty tops
literally flying around the ring!

256
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
It's a terrifying whirlwind
of spinning tops!

257
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
But Gon is evading all of them!

258
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
With all of his tops already in play,

259
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Gido can only watch with the rest of us!

260
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
[yells] No, not that way!

261
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Oh, no! There’s nowhere to run!

262
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
[grunts]

263
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[Wing] That situation could very well
have cost him his life

264
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
and he was enjoying it?

265
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[Killua] Yeah. And I would know.

266
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,000
I’ve felt the same way before myself.

267
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
But at least I pick and choose my battles.

268
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Once he’s in the zone,

269
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
he loses sight of everything else.

270
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Oh! But he’s not the type
to break the same promise twice,

271
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
so don't worry.

272
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[Wing] Oh, dear.

273
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
What have I done?

274
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,000
[Killua] It's too late.

275
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,000
We already know all the facts.

276
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Gon and me both.

277
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
If you regret teaching us
and want to back out,

278
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
we’ll find somebody else.

279
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Or we’ll simply learn it ourselves.

280
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
You don't have to feel responsible.

281
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
My brother can use Nen.

282
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Hisoka can, too.

283
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
So Gon and I were bound
to find out about it eventually.

284
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
I understand.

285
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
I intend to finish what I started.

286
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
There are so many more things
that I have yet to teach you.

287
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Zushi is waiting in my room.

288
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
You can train with him, if you’d like.

289
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Killua] Nah. I’ll pass.

290
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Hm?

291
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I don't want to leave Gon behind.

292
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
If he can keep his promise,

293
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
we’ll train together.

294
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Give him a message for me, then!

295
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Tell him I will let him
practice the other ‘Nen’, the flame!

296
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
And tell him to work on Ten daily!

297
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Hey, Gon.

298
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[Wing] Master...

299
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,000
It was never my intention, but…

300
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,000
have I…

301
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Have I awoken a terrible monster?

302
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,000
[Zushi] Master?

303
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[Kurapika] What’s going on?

304
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,000
[Rei] You found this agency on your own,

305
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
and that tells me you’re pretty sharp.

306
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Even so…

307
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
I can’t introduce you
to our valued clients.

308
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
And it’s not because
of your total lack of experience.

309
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Some of our clients
don’t seem to mind that.

310
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
The thing is...

311
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
experience isn’t all you lack.

312
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,000
But what do you mean?

313
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Like I told you,
I already have a Hunter’s License.

314
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[Rei] Maybe. But your Exam isn’t over yet.

315
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
It’s obvious.

316
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Excuse me?

317
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
-[Rei] Can you see anything?
-Huh?

318
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Like next to me, I mean.

319
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Can’t see a thing, can you?

320
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
You come back when you can...

321
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
and not before.

322
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
That’s the minimum requirement here.

323
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,000
What does she mean?

324
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:01,000
What is it that I can’t see?

325
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[thunder rolling]

326
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
[electricity buzzes]

327
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[man] You can’t see it,
but you can sense it, huh?

328
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
-[Kurapika] Why did you do that?
-[man] This?

329
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Oh. I was just playing around.

330
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
[thunder]

331
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
This must be fate,

332
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
us crossing paths. Y’think?

333
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Try to think of this as...

334
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
a little bit of friendly advice
from a senior.

335
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
You didn’t notice when I stole this,

336
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
or when I walked right past you, either.

337
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,000
You’re totally clueless.

338
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Bastard!
Give me back my license right now!

339
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Does a newbie who knows nothing of Nen

340
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
have a chance of beating me?

341
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
Nen, huh?

342
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,000
[scoffs]

343
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:37,000
[thunder]

344
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Wanna give it a try?

345
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[rain patters]

346
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
[Kurapika panting]

347
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Do you get it now?

348
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
There’s something important
you still lack.

349
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,000
[Kurapika grunts] I...

350
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
I need...

351
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,000
[shouts]
I need enough power to fight on my own!

352
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
[man] Come with me.

353
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:20,000
I’ll teach you.

354
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:26,000
The real exam has just begun.

355
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
[narrator] Gon’s hidden potential
is beginning to awaken.

356
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
And Kurapika
has also encountered a new power.

357
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
One that he hopes
will help propel him forward.

358
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[theme song playing]

359
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
[Gon] Coming up:

360
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

361
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

362
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

363
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

364
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Today, we're introducing
the Hunter Agency!

365
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
This place helps pro Hunters find work,

366
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,000
but it was really hard for Kurapika
to find the office that he visited.

367
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:11,000
Gotta find the agency
before you qualify as a pro Hunter.

368
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,000
[Gon] Next time:

369
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Destiny x and x Tenacity.

370
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
[Killua]
I wonder who Four-Eyes is, anyway?

371
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Gon] Hmm...
I wonder who the Floor Masters are.

372
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Killua gasps]

373
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
[Killua and Gon] Could it be?!
